  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., prices dropping from ~74 to ~66) followed by neutral sentiment; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10%.",
    "When sentiment history contains a spike of +1.0 or -1.0 within the last 3 days, the model fails to capture immediate volatility and instead predicts a smooth linear trend, missing sharp spikes in both directions.",
    "Forecasts show significant mean reversion lag: after a sudden price spike (e.g., >76), the model continues its upward trajectory while true outcomes immediately reverse and decline.",
    "In low-volatility periods with flat sentiment history, the model over-smooths data, resulting in forecasts that drift away from actual jagged price paths within the first 5 days of the horizon.",
    "Systematic error pattern: Model assumes monotonic growth during recovery phases but fails to account for mean-reverting corrections that occur within 7-10 days."
  ]
}
